  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Thomas asked whether there is an argument embedded in the question about the applicable standard."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked if, assuming no unique standard in the school context, the court on remand would decide which standard is appropriate."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked for the difference between \u201cdeliberate indifference\u201d as defined by the Solicitor General and \u201cbad faith\u201d or \u201cgross misjudgment.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor questioned the source of the tests, noting that mens rea is generally willfulness, which the statute does not mention."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Barrett asked whether other circuits have taken the view, indicating it may be a live issue in the lower courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked if the Solicitor General\u2019s formulation of deliberate indifference was acceptable."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked what impulse led many lower courts to adopt a standard the Court finds unsupported."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "MS. REAVES",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 45,
              "start": 45
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Ms. Reaves testified that there was enough to go to trial because of deliberate indifference after repeated requests for an interpreter."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether the IDEA\u2019s requirement to provide a free appropriate public education could be \u201cextremely expensive.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 50,
              "start": 50
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked what could properly happen below if the dual\u2011track approach is rejected and no standards for damages or injunctions are set."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 52,
              "start": 52
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh asked how the Court should deal with the lack of clear notice when the Solicitor General frames deliberate indifference as requiring actual knowledge of a substantially likely violation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 64,
              "start": 64
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Gorsuch asked whether Mr. Martinez and the Solicitor General are lying."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 66,
              "start": 66
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson asked for at least one other circuit that has applied the bad\u2011faith standard in a different context."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 67,
              "start": 67
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Barrett, justice Barrett noted that such a change would be a \u201csea change.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 69,
              "start": 69
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justice Kavanaugh clarified that the definition of \u201cbad faith\u201d does not require animus."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice JACKSON",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 74,
              "start": 74
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Jackson, justice Jackson restated the question presented: whether the ADA and Rehabilitation Act require a uniquely stringent bad\u2011faith or gross\u2011misjudgment standard for relief."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0003-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 85,
              "start": 85
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor observed that nowhere else has \u201cdeliberate indifference\u201d or \u201cgross indifference\u201d been used to define intentional discrimination."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 88,
              "start": 88
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor noted that intent was not an issue because the plaintiffs already obtained an injunction under the IDEA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "9ff217544eaa600f5a4affe18328f5dff3eeb994de13d39f620867af13a9afcb",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-9ff217544eaa-0004-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 97,
              "start": 97
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kavanaugh, justice Kavanaugh questioned how one can know a federally protected right was substantially likely to be violated without knowing what the law provides."
      }
    ],
